faq:
  - q: How Much Does An Oil Change Cost vs. Skipping It?
    body: >-
      Every oil change at Duft Auto includes a written estimate before the filter comes off, so the exact cost is clear before work begins. A routine oil and filter change costs far less than the repair bill that follows extended engine wear from a skipped or delayed interval. Full synthetic oil carries a higher per-service price than conventional oil, offset by a longer interval between changes. Duft Auto reviews oil type and interval directly with each customer, matching the service to the vehicle's manufacturer specification rather than defaulting to the highest-priced option. Skipping an oil change to save money in the short term risks a far larger repair cost tied to accelerated internal engine wear.
  - q: How Do I Know My Vehicle Needs An Oil Change?
    items:
      - Oil change or maintenance light on the dashboard
      - Oil appears low on the dipstick
      - Engine noise or reduced performance
      - Approaching or past the manufacturer's mileage interval
      - Oil looks gritty or smells burnt
  - q: What Does The Oil Change Process Involve At Duft Auto?
    body: >-
      An oil change appointment starts with a scheduled bay time, confirmed in advance by phone, text, or email. Auggie drains the old oil, replaces the oil filter, and refills the engine with the oil type specified for the vehicle, whether full synthetic, synthetic blend, or conventional. A multi-point inspection runs alongside the oil service, covering tire tread, brake pads, and fluid levels. Findings get explained directly, in plain language, before any additional work gets recommended. Most oil change appointments complete within a single service window, since the appointment-only model allocates bay time and parts in advance. A written summary of the service and any inspection findings goes to the customer before they leave.
  - q: Vehicles Duft Auto Services For Oil Changes
    items:
      - Domestic and import passenger vehicles — sedans, hatchbacks, and coupes needing routine synthetic or conventional oil service
      - Pickup trucks and SUVs, including diesel models requiring diesel-specific oil and filters
      - Daily drivers and family vehicles across Chilliwack, Sardis, Yarrow, and Rosedale
      - High-mileage vehicles needing seal-conditioning oil formulated for engines with extended service history
